  "claim": "The director of Delovak Athara has had a greater impact on French culture than the director of À propos de Nice. À propos de Nice is a 1930 silent short documentary film photographed by Boris Kaufman.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Lester James Peries. Sentence: Sri Lankabhimanya Lester James Peries (Sinhala: ශ්‍රී ලංකාභිමාන්‍ය ලෙස්ටර් ජේම්ස් පීරිස්) (born 5 April 1919) is an internationally acclaimed Sri Lankan film director, screenwriter, and film producer.\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: An active filmmaker since 1949, Peries has been involved in over 28 films, including shorts and documentaries.\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: He has received critical acclaim for directing \"Rekava\", \"Gamperaliya\", \"Nidhanaya\", \"Golu Hadawatha\", \"Kaliyugaya\", \"Awaragira\" and \"Yuganthaya\".\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: His movie \"Wekande Walauwa\", starring Ravindra Randeniya and Malini Fonseka, was Sri Lanka's first ever submission for the Academy Awards.\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: Peries' films often deal with Sri Lankan family life in rural settings and conflicted characters.\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: He helped create an authentic expression of Sinhala Cinema.\nPage: Jean Vigo. Sentence: Jean Vigo (] ; 26 April 1905 – 5 October 1934) was a French film director who helped establish poetic realism in film in the 1930s; he was a posthumous influence on the French New Wave of the late 1950s and early 1960s.\nPage: Delovak Athara. Sentence: Delovak Athara (Sinhala, \"Between Two Worlds\") is a 1966 Sri Lankan drama film directed by Dr. Lester James Peries, the screen play dialoug and script by Dr. Tissa Abeysekara.\nPage: À propos de Nice. Sentence: À propos de Nice is a 1930 silent short documentary film directed by Jean Vigo and photographed by Boris Kaufman.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Lester James Peries. Sentence: Sri Lankabhimanya Lester James Peries (Sinhala: ශ්‍රී ලංකාභිමාන්‍ය ලෙස්ටර් ජේම්ස් පීරිස්) (born 5 April 1919) is an internationally acclaimed Sri Lankan film director, screenwriter, and film producer.\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: An active filmmaker since 1949, Peries has been involved in over 28 films, including shorts and documentaries.\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: He has received critical acclaim for directing \"Rekava\", \"Gamperaliya\", \"Nidhanaya\", \"Golu Hadawatha\", \"Kaliyugaya\", \"Awaragira\" and \"Yuganthaya\".\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: His movie \"Wekande Walauwa\", starring Ravindra Randeniya and Malini Fonseka, was Sri Lanka's first ever submission for the Academy Awards.\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: Peries' films often deal with Sri Lankan family life in rural settings and conflicted characters.\nPage: Lester James Peries. Sentence: He helped create an authentic expression of Sinhala Cinema.\nPage: Jean Vigo. Sentence: Jean Vigo (] ; 26 April 1905 – 5 October 1934) was a French film director who helped establish poetic realism in film in the 1930s; he was a posthumous influence on the French New Wave of the late 1950s and early 1960s.\nPage: Delovak Athara. Sentence: Delovak Athara (Sinhala, \"Between Two Worlds\") is a 1966 Sri Lankan drama film directed by Dr. Lester James Peries, the screen play dialoug and script by Dr. Tissa Abeysekara.\nPage: À propos de Nice. Sentence: À propos de Nice is a 1930 silent short documentary film directed by Jean Vigo and photographed by Boris Kaufman.",
