        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6d0e61ea-a16a-54c7-8744-0b916544d6f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lester James Peries, Jean Vigo, Tissa Abeysekara, Boris Kaufman, Ravindra Randeniya, Malini Fonseka\n- Works: Rekava, Gamperaliya, Nidhanaya, Golu Hadawatha, Kaliyugaya, Awaragira, Yuganthaya, Wekande Walauwa, Delovak Athara, À propos de Nice\n- Topics: Sinhala cinema, poetic realism, French New Wave, Sri Lankan family life in rural settings\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Vigo was born on 26 April 1905 and died on 5 October 1934.\n- Jean Vigo was a French film director who helped establish poetic realism in film in the 1930s and later influenced the French New Wave of the late 1950s and early 1960s.\n- À propos de Nice is a 1930 silent short documentary film directed by Jean Vigo and photographed by Boris Kaufman.\n- Lester James Peries was born on 5 April 1919 and is a Sri Lankan film director, screenwriter, and film producer.\n- Lester James Peries had been active as a filmmaker since 1949 and was involved in more than 28 films, including shorts and documentaries.\n- Delovak Athara is a 1966 Sri Lankan drama film directed by Lester James Peries, with screenplay, dialogue, and script by Tissa Abeysekara.\n- Lester James Peries received critical acclaim for directing Rekava, Gamperaliya, Nidhanaya, Golu Hadawatha, Kaliyugaya, Awaragira, and Yuganthaya.\n- Wekande Walauwa, a film by Lester James Peries starring Ravindra Randeniya and Malini Fonseka, was Sri Lanka's first submission for the Academy Awards.\n- Lester James Peries's films often portray Sri Lankan family life in rural settings and conflicted characters.\n- Lester James Peries helped create an authentic expression of Sinhala cinema.",
